    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nWhen inside a function with multiple arguments I expect `[n]daa` to delete the `n` two arguments.\r\nBut it only deletes that last (n-th) argument of `[n]daa]`.\n\n### Neovim version\n\nv0.10.2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Install mini.ai\r\n2. Open reproduce.lua\r\n ```lua\r\nfunction(foo, ba<CURSOR HERE>r, baz)\r\n\r\nend\r\n```\r\n3. `2daa`\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n ```lua\r\nfunction(foo)\r\n\r\nend\r\n```\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n ```lua\r\nfunction(foo, bar)\r\n\r\nend\r\n```",
