            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I am afraid this is how \"argument\" textobject works. It is documented [in the help](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/7ebfab26d77a4b9b05aaae565907e7fa4b2ee154/doc/mini-ai.txt#L165C24-L165C39): when pressing `v2ia` it selects \"next\" argument and not both.\r\n\r\nThe reason for this is that it is an \"argument\" textobject and not \"argument**s**\", so it is designed to select only single argument at a time.\r\n\r\nMoreover, when user executes textobject with `[count]`, it behaves [as if consecutive application was done in Visual mode](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/7ebfab26d77a4b9b05aaae565907e7fa4b2ee154/doc/mini-ai.txt#L129-L131) (so for `2aa` it is like pressing `aa` followed by another `aa`). Selecting \"second next\" argument works here because default `config.search_method` is `'cover_or_next'` and second consecutive application selects next argument (because there is no covering one as \"argument\" textobject doesn't support that). If search method were `'cover'`, there will be a warning about not being able to find the second textobject.\r\n\r\nAll in all, it works as expected (and documented). Hope this helps clarifying the reasoning.",
